WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.775
Why does this chapter exist?

2
00:00:01.775 --> 00:00:06.699
Because the program's last gates ask for
things a single snapshot can't give: a

3
00:00:06.699 --> 00:00:12.013
Tier 0 drift handled as an incident, and
evidence for every elevation in the period.

4
00:00:12.013 --> 00:00:15.262
Book 04 already says what
goes in the package.

5
00:00:15.262 --> 00:00:18.300
Learn supplies the two
facts the design turns on.

6
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.207
First, the audit log
only keeps thirty days,

7
00:00:21.207 --> 00:00:24.612
so evidence has to be
collected before it ages out.

8
00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:29.288
Second, one activation can show
up under several correlation IDs,

9
00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:31.626
but its request ID never changes.

10
00:00:31.626 --> 00:00:33.980
That request ID becomes the key.
